      "RegenerateResponse": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "POST /v1/meetings/{id}/summary/regenerate (T-12b) response body -\nreturned with 202 Accepted, since the summary is generated by a\nbackground task (see SummaryService::process_transcript_background).\nT28a: a regeneration has ONE identity, `operation_id`, minted at acceptance\n(before its preparation, so a preparation failure is reported against it\nand never as a 202). `run_id` is null at acceptance - no run exists yet -\nand `state` is `preparing`. `status_url`/`wait_url` are the operation's own\nroutes (T28b; they 404 until it lands). `process_id` is the pre-T28a field,\nkept for one release as a duplicate of `meeting_id`.",
        "required": [
          "operation_id",
          "app_instance_id",
          "meeting_id",
          "state",
          "status_url",
          "wait_url",
          "process_id"
